course: dictionary
lesson: 4568
title: Heedless and careless
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Heedless means not paying attention, so you miss a warning or a danger. It is close to careless, but heedless often means you do not even stop to think. «What a conceited and heedless ass!» The speaker is cross with someone who does not notice what is around them or does not care what might happen.
explain: Look at the words near heedless for clues. In «heedless of the danger», the words after of tell you what is being ignored. Swap in your meaning: "not paying attention to the danger" still makes sense, so you have understood it.
explain: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad is heedless of his friends' warnings and drives too fast. He does not listen to the warnings, and that gets him into trouble. Stories often show heedless characters getting into trouble, so watch for what happens next.
fact: Heedless means not paying attention, especially to a warning or a danger.
fact: «Heedless of» means without thinking about something: «heedless of the danger».
fact: Heedless is close to careless, but it often means ignoring a warning without a thought.
fact: «A heedless rush» means hurrying without looking out for what might go wrong.
fact: Being heedless near roads, water or fire is dangerous, so always stop and think first.
exercise: «What a conceited and heedless ass!» What does heedless mean here? | Kind and gentle to everyone | Loud and cheerful | Very clever and quick to learn | *Not paying attention to what is around
exercise: Toad is heedless of his friends' warnings and drives too fast. What is the problem with Toad? | He is always on time | *He does not pay attention to the warnings | He is scared of the dark | He is too quiet for anyone to hear him
exercise: Which phrase is the best swap for heedless in «a heedless rush»? | Slow and very careful | Happy and calm | Quiet and shy | *Hurried, without looking out for danger
test: Which sentence shows someone being heedless? | She read the warning sign and stepped back. | He put out the candle before he left. | He sat quietly and waited for the bus. | *He ran across the busy road without looking.
test: What does «heedless of the danger» mean? | Running away from the danger | Telling everyone about the danger | *Not thinking about the danger | Thinking very hard about the danger
exam: Why is being heedless near water or fire dangerous? | It makes the water warmer | Fire only burns when you are calm | *It makes you ignore warnings, and you can get hurt | It is never dangerous
